WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:07.110
Hi, I’m Michael. Welcome to the Form Your Team facilitation course.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:15.390
For more than fourteen years, I’ve worked with teams and leaders on how they work together, and one thing keeps coming back.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.210
Great teams don’t happen by accident.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:25.450
They stand on a strong foundation, and that foundation is built in a few honest conversations.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:36.310
You probably already know the free toolkit on formyourteam.dk: six conversations, each with a few key questions and a simple exercise.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:48.390
This course is about the part that the website can’t give you: how to actually run those conversations with your own team, so that they feel natural, honest and useful.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.310
This course is made for team leads and informal leaders.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.890
You don’t need to have any particular facilitation experience.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:04.290
You need a team, a little time, and the willingness to ask questions that you don’t already know the answers to.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:14.890
Here is how it works. First, a short module on facilitating your own team, because leading and facilitating at the same time is its own skill.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:26.030
Then one module for each of the six conversations: why it matters, how to run the exercise step by step, and what to do when things get tricky.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.210
We finish with how to plan your series and keep it alive afterwards.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.270
Every lesson is short.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.350
Each one ends with a few takeaways and one small thing to try.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.490
Download the canvases and the workbook, and keep them next to you as we go.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:56.610
By the end, you’ll be able to run all six conversations with confidence, handle the awkward moments, and turn what your team says into agreements that actually change how you work together.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:57.028
Let’s begin.

